      "html": "~"
    },
    {
      "id": "da980942-d791-4fb9-b561-a7aaaf62e241",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "189c910f-6dcc-400e-8ab6-4a07c03be497",
      "type": "quote",
      "html": "“Playing a game is the voluntary attempt to overcome unnecessary obstacles.”<br>~<strong><a href=\"#/bernard-suits\">Bernard Suits</a></strong>, <a href=\"#/the-grasshopper\"><em>The Grasshopper: Games, Life, &amp; Utopia</em></a>"
    },
    {
      "id": "80f7bb42-fdeb-445b-a102-dd0dd5b68659",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "9f156046-aa5b-4c89-9d1f-14295afe2691",
      "type": "quote",
      "html": "“A videogame is a fast drifting-vibrating book which takes the geometrical mechanic of e.g. Spinoza’s Ethics and automates a reading-path through it, repeating passages, linking to other, flowing down lines, bifurcations, etc. meanwhile being made sensible through its inputs-outputs, which futher modulate/transform the automatic-reading paths being followed.”<br>~<a href=\"#/david-kanaga\"><strong>David Kanaga</strong></a>,<em> Structure &amp; Alchemy in New Fractal Playspaces</em>"
    },
    {
      "id": "7246b7db-4faf-4886-b4d2-3880fe5144d5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "eba11775-c317-4e22-9c45-e111a4824a03",
      "type": "quote",
      "html": "“A game is simply any interaction between agent and environment, where the agent’s goals or preferences transform the environment into sets of obstacles and affordances.”<br>~<strong>Suspended Reason</strong>, <a href=\"#/gaming-and-entailment\">Gaming &amp; entailment</a>"
    },
    {
      "id": "1d8354da-1a17-4b17-873a-6abe5bbfc409",
      "type": "paragraph",
